  "annotation": "Positive videos show material flame or a persistent smoke-like plume at the start of the selected view. Zero refers to the start of the clip. The smoke positives include recorded demonstrations. Negatives retain the archive label, without independent per-frame annotations. Two source positives show fire in an ordinary fireplace and were reclassified as contextual negatives. Each camera and scene can appear more than once among the source negatives. Two obvious near-duplicate positive views were excluded by visual inspection. This is a development/transfer corpus. Its classifications do not claim a known ignition time or operational false-alert rates.",
  "preprocess": "Source frame timing preserved, no audio, at most 960 pixels wide, even height, yuv420p H.264 with one libx264 thread and fast preset, native timestamps.",
  "exclusions": {
    "flame-posVideo9.878.avi": "Fire is visible throughout. Camera zoom prevents a fixed controlled-region comparison.",
    "smoke-testpos05.821.avi": "Published source contains a prior detection overlay, which can confound an independent visual comparison.",
    "smoke-testpos03.819.avi": "Same camera and setting as flame-posVideo7.876.avi.",
    "smoke-testpos07.823.avi": "Same camera and setting as smoke-testpos06.822.avi."
  },
